# deploy/host/ufw/extra.list — every UFW rule of the main server that is neither a
# module's nor ssh's, and every public listener that is closed on purpose
# (docs/host-state.md#the-firewall-ufw).
#
#   role|rule|reason
#
#   role    main (a relay has no UFW: its input filter is vpnrelay_input)
#   rule    a ufw rule exactly as `ufw show added` prints it, without "ufw " and
#           without a comment — vpn-bot-ufw-apply adds it with comment 'vpn-bot:extra':
#             main|allow 8080/tcp|<why>
#             main|allow from 203.0.113.7 to any port 9100 proto tcp|<why>
#             main|route allow in on wg1 out on eth0 from 10.9.0.0/24|<why>
#           or `closed <port>/<tcp|udp>`: something listens there on a public or
#           wildcard address and the firewall keeps it closed on purpose (the deploy's
#           listener check fails on a public TCP listener that is neither allowed nor
#           declared closed):
#             main|closed 8443/tcp|<why>
#   reason  why, in at least 20 characters
#
# The module rules (Xray, Hysteria2, SOCKS5, subscription, MTProto, AWG) and the ssh
# port come from .env and the module table — never list them here. Measured on
# 2026-11-12 every rule and public listener of the main server is a module's or ssh's:
# nothing goes here.
